begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$" 13194139534989 17592186045417 true] [17592186447024 1072 #uuid "47833d2d-e4b4-5480-a72b-ba5cccc746dd" 13194139534989 17592186045417 true] [17592186447024 1074 "Using the usual formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-(-4)}{0}=\\frac{y-5}{3}=\\frac{z-1}{2}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nor equivalently\n\n$$\n\\frac{x+4}{0}=\\frac{y-5}{3}=\\frac{z-1}{2},\n$$\n\nwhich is problematic because $\\frac{x+4}{0}$ involves division by zero.\n\nHowever, notice that in our line, the $x$ component always maintains the constant value of $x=-4:$\n\n$$\nr=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 5+3t \\\\ 1+2t\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$\n\nSo, in the Cartesian equation, we remove the $\\frac{x+4}{0}$ part and instead write $x=-4$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{y-5}{3}=\\frac{z-1}{2},\\,x=-4\n$$" 13194139534989 17592186045417 true] [17592186447025 1068 #edb/ref 17592186447023 13194139534989 17592186045417 true] [17592186447025 1069 "q-127468" 13194139534989 17592186045417 true] [17592186447025 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534989 17592186045417 true] [17592186447025 1071 "![](images/01/01943e80947c833ef37241fb836db96afd61731b9873cd061277a7453b34f3d8.png)\n\nFind a Cartesian equation of the line shown in the figure above." 13194139534989 17592186045417 true] [17592186447025 1072 #uuid "61ab7a4c-ae26-516b-9967-3f8072e6be8b" 13194139534989 17592186045417 true] [17592186447025 1074 "We know that the line passes through the points $P(-1,3,7)$ and $Q(3,-1,1).$ Now, we need to find a vector parallel to the given line. Let's consider the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ which is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨3,-1,1⟩-⟨-1,3,7⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,-4,-6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the point $P$ and the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$, we have that the Cartesian (canonical) equation of the given line is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-(-1)}{4}=\\frac{y-3}{-4}=\\frac{z-7}{-6}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nor equivalently\n\n$$\n\\frac{x+1}{4}=\\frac{y-3}{-4}=\\frac{z-7}{-6}.\n$$" 13194139534989 17592186045417 true] [17592186447026 1062 #uuid "6c98daf6-3ae9-572b-ac90-c2ddf8f54388" 13194139534989 17592186045417 true] [17592186447026 1063 #edb/ref 17592186262792 13194139534989 17592186045417 true] [17592186447027 1058 #edb/ref 17592186447028 13194139534989 17592186045417 true] [17592186447027 1062 #uuid "819efd4e-ea7b-530c-8492-698aae4bfae3" 13194139534989 17592186045417 true] [17592186447027 1063 #edb/ref 17592186338882 13194139534989 17592186045417 true] [17592186447028 1058 #edb/ref 17592186447030 13194139534989 17592186045417 true] [17592186447028 1062 #uuid "842ff690-e68c-5ec7-a29c-4509d3d2ffad" 13194139534989 17592186045417 true] [17592186447028 1063 #edb/ref 17592186447024 13194139534989 17592186045417 true] [17592186447029 1058 #edb/ref 17592186447026 13194139534989 17592186045417 true] [17592186447029 1062 #uuid "aaebba90-5fd2-5222-b798-afec0cfd305e" 13194139534989 17592186045417 true] [17592186447029 1063 #edb/ref 17592186447025 13194139534989 17592186045417 true] [17592186447030 1058 #edb/ref 17592186447029 13194139534989 17592186045417 true] [17592186447030 1062 #uuid "e724c68f-5680-5be4-aa66-0e3b05d39d11" 13194139534989 17592186045417 true] [17592186447030 1063 #edb/ref 17592186367226 13194139534989 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"activity-4c26b5f1-ca5b-5728-8463-5b32e35af136" 17592186447011 "answer-2bbe3ab9-a7ef-5513-96b0-4bb81eecfdf5" 17592186447012 "answer-34899314-00b5-5497-adbb-b71a1ac21237" 17592186447013 "answer-3aff6a90-29cb-5fbb-a280-7d4c79fc7881" 17592186447014 "answer-58eab78c-4412-5b45-b6ad-1d2c084a66a9" 17592186447015 "answer-6083d104-e8d5-54a9-91d4-825774ce35f9" 17592186447016 "answer-7287e364-e5ae-5892-9f4f-1be7926ae48e" 17592186447017 "answer-77cf8edb-f11a-593d-b22b-70517358473d" 17592186447018 "answer-a3f8e739-90fc-54a0-8ff2-caa9d9c9da58" 17592186447019 "answer-bd35653f